.TITLE "sips"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Processes images using the Scriptable Image Processing System on macOS.
This command-line utility allows for various image manipulations, including
resizing, rotating, flipping, changing format, and extracting/modifying
metadata. It is a powerful tool for batch processing image files.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**imageproc**

.DIV "TLDR"
**sips -Z 1024 __image.png__**
Resizes __image.png__ to fit within a 1024-pixel square, preserving aspect ratio.
> __image.png__: The input image file.

**sips -s format __jpeg__ __image.png__ --out __image.jpg__**
Converts __image.png__ to JPEG format and saves it as __image.jpg__.
> __jpeg__: The output format (e.g., jpeg, png, tiff). | __image.png__: The input image file. | __image.jpg__: The output image file.

**sips -r 90 __image.png__**
Rotates __image.png__ by 90 degrees clockwise.
> __image.png__: The input image file.

**sips -g pixelWidth __image.png__**
Gets the pixel width of __image.png__.
> __pixelWidth__: The property to retrieve. | __image.png__: The input image file.

**sips -i __image.png__**
Adds ICC profile to __image.png__.
> __image.png__: The input image file.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
`sips` is invaluable for automating image processing tasks on macOS.
It can handle a wide range of formats and operations, making it suitable
for scripting repetitive graphic manipulations. Always test commands
on copies of important images to avoid accidental data loss.

